We can rewrite the sum as an arithmetic series and use the formula for the sum of a geometric series.

Let $S = \displaystyle\sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1 + , \omega^k + . \omega^{2k} + \omega^{3k}}.$
We have

\begin{align*}
S &= \displaystyle\sum_{k = 0}^{1727} \frac{1}{1 + \omega^{k} + \omega^{2k} + \omega^{3k}}  - \frac{1}{1 + \omega^0}\\
&= \displaystyle\sum_{k = 0}^{1727} \frac{1}{1 + \omega^{k} + \omega^{2k} + \omega^{3k}}  - \frac{1}{4}.
\end{align*}

Notice that $\omega^{1728} = 1,$ so $\omega^{1729} = \omega.$ Then we have

\begin{align*}
1 + \omega^{k} + \omega^{2k} + \omega^{3k} &= (1 + \omega + \omega^2)(1 + \omega^{1729k})\\
&= (1 + \omega + \omega^2)(1 + \omega^{(1729 - 1)k})(1 + \omega) \\
&= (1 + \omega + \omega^2)(1 - \omega^{1728})(1 + \omega).
\end{align*}

Hence,

\begin{align*}
S &= \frac{1}{4} + \displaystyle\sum_{k = 0}^{1727} \frac{1}{(1 + \omega + \omega^2)(1 - \omega^{1728})(1 + \omega)} \\
&= \frac{1}{4} + \displaystyle\sum_{k = 0}^{1727} \frac{\omega^{1728}}{(1 - \omega)(1 - \omega^{1729})(1 - \omega^{2})(1 + \omega^{1728k + 1})}\\
&= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{\omega^{1728}}{(1 - \omega)(1 - \omega^{1729})(1 - \omega^{2})} \displaystyle\sum_{k = 0}^{\infty} \frac{1}{(1 - \omega^{1728k + 1})}\\
\end{align*}

The harmonic series $\displaystyle\sum_{k = 0}^{\infty} \frac{1}{1 - \omega^{1728k + 1}}$ diverges. However, since $\omega^{1729}= \omega$, the recurring sum will telescope, leaving us with only finitely many terms. Let's calculate it:

\begin{align*}
S &= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{\omega^{1728}}{(1 - \omega)(1 - \omega^{1729})(1 - \omega^{2})} \left[ \frac{1}{1 - \omega} + \frac{1}{\omega - \omega^2} + \frac{1}{\omega - \omega^4} + \cdots \right] \\
&= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{\omega^{1728}}{(1 - \omega)(1 - \omega^{1729})(1 - \omega^{2})} \left[ \frac{1}{1 - \omega} - \frac{1}{1 - \omega^2} + \frac{1}{1 - \omega^4} - \cdots \right] \\
&= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{\omega^{1728}}{(1 - \omega)(1 - \omega^{1729})(1 - \omega^{2})} \left[ \frac{1}{1 - \omega} - \left(\frac{1}{1 - \omega^{1729}} + \frac{1}{1 - \omega^{3458}} + \frac{1}{1 - \omega^{5197}} + \cdots \right) \right] \\
&= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{728} \left[ \frac{\omega^{1728}}{\omega - 1} - \left(\frac{\omega^{3458}}{\omega - \omega^{1729}} + \frac{\omega^{5197}}{\omega - \omega^{3458}} + \cdots \right) \right] \\
&= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{728} \left[ \frac{\omega^{1728}}{\omega - 1} - \frac{1}{\omega - 1} + \frac{1}{\omega - 1} \right] \\
&= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{728} (\omega^{1728} - 1) \\
\end{align*}

Again making use of the property $\omega^{1729} = \omega$, we find

