 & 4473 \mod 1000 \\
 &= 473 \mod 1000\\
 &= 73 \mod 1000\\
 &= 73 \quad (\text{there is no remainder when dividing by 1000})
\end{align*}

Now, the thousands digit of the square of $2011$ is the double digit formed by the tens and units digits of $73$.

We can write:
\begin{equation*}
\boxed{2011^{2011} \dots}
\end{equation*}

